      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](go/traj/b7470b1e-c66a-4709-b1d6-581a70553b7e)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The build system changes are correct. Creating symlinks to the local checkout\u0027s headers in `$(out)/include/chromeos/ec/` and prepending `-I$(out)/include` to `HOST_CPPFLAGS` ensures that host utilities (e.g., `ectool`) resolve to the local headers over the system headers. The use of Make\u0027s order-only prerequisites (`| $(chromeos-ec-headers)`) perfectly handles the build order: it guarantees the symlinks are present when the compiler is first invoked, allowing the compiler\u0027s `-MMD` flag to correctly populate the `.d` file for future dependency tracking, without causing unnecessary rebuilds. The `#ifndef` header guard cleanup safely removes the old transitional logic.\n*   **Security:** No security implications.\n*   **Style:** The Makefile changes use idiomatic practices, such as `$(@D)` and `$(abspath $\u003c)`, and safely capture the environment flags (like `HOST_CFLAGS`) prior to prepending the local include paths. The header guard changes are straightforward and clean.\n*   **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** The manual test specified in the description (`make build/host/util/ectool`) is the right approach to verify these build system and header resolution changes.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL is well-scoped to addressing the host tools header resolution issue and the associated header guard cleanup.",
