      "message": "Hardcoding `@mkdir` and `@ln` suppresses command output even when building with `make V\u003d1` (used in verbose Portage/CQ build logs) and duplicates the recipe between the pattern rule and the explicit `cros_ec_dev.h` rule.\n\nConsider using `$(call quiet,...)` (or `$(Q)`) to align with the rest of `Makefile.rules`:\n```makefile\ncmd_symlink_hdr \u003d mkdir -p $(@D) \u0026\u0026 ln -sf $(abspath $\u003c) $@\n\n$(out)/include/chromeos/ec/%: include/%\n\t$(call quiet,symlink_hdr,SYMLINK)\n\n$(out)/include/chromeos/ec/cros_ec_dev.h: util/cros_ec_dev.h\n\t$(call quiet,symlink_hdr,SYMLINK)\n```",
