      "writtenOn": "2026-09-16T21:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Modifying `include/ec_commands.h` (or any other header) in an incremental build (`make build/host/util/ectool` or Portage\u0027s `CROS_WORKON_INCREMENTAL_BUILD\u003d1` in `ec-utils-9999.ebuild`) updates the symlink in `$(out)/include/chromeos/ec/`, but does not recompile `ectool` or other host utilities.\n\nThis happens because:\n1. `| $(chromeos-ec-headers)` is an order-only prerequisite, so GNU Make only checks that the symlinks exist and ignores their timestamps once created.\n2. Although `cmd_c_to_host` and `cmd_cxx_to_host` pass `-MMD -MF $@.d -MT $@` to generate `.d` dependency files, `deps` in `Makefile` only includes `$(ro-deps) $(rw-deps) $(deps-y)` and never includes `$(host-utils:\u003d.d)` or `$(host-utils-cxx:\u003d.d)`.\n\nAdding the host utility `.d` files to `deps` (and `-MP` to `cmd_c_to_host` / `cmd_cxx_to_host`) ensures incremental builds properly recompile host tools whenever any header changes:\n```makefile\ndeps +\u003d $(addsuffix .d, $(host-utils) $(host-utils-cxx))\n-include $(deps)\n```",
